@@ -162,13 +162,25 @@ contracts:
       When not decorative, Avatar provides accessible name:
       - If alt prop provided: uses alt text
       - If no alt prop (iOS/Android): "User avatar" for human, "AI agent avatar" for agent
-      - Web requires alt prop when src is provided
+      - Web requires alt prop when src is provided, and emits a development warning when it
+        is missing. The warning fires iff: type is 'human' AND src is provided AND alt is
+        absent AND decorative is false.
+        - Agent type is out of scope: agent ignores src entirely (no image renders), so no
+          alt is needed and no warning fires.
+        - decorative=true suppresses the warning: it is the supported signal that the avatar
+          is intentionally non-informative (aria-hidden="true"), so alt text would never be
+          announced.
+        - "Absent" alt means getAttribute('alt') === null. Only setAttribute('alt', '')
+          yields a genuinely empty alt (no warning); the alt property setter treats '' as
+          falsy and removes the attribute, so `avatar.alt = ''` collapses to absent and does
+          warn. iOS and Android likewise collapse empty alt to absent.
     wcag: "1.1.1 Non-text Content"
     platforms: [web, ios, android]
     validation:
       - Alt text matches alt prop when provided
       - Default label used when no alt prop (native)
       - Accessible name present for non-decorative avatars
+      - Web dev warning fires only for human + src + absent alt + non-decorative
     test_approach: |
       - Render Avatar with alt="John Doe"
       - Verify accessible name is "John Doe"
